    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0123" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg13"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/510a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-10T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 10,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>47. House of Representatives approved Greek Debt Settlement today. Senate action
                    expected shortly.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d19-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d19-f1" n="15" xml:id="d19-f1-content">
                <p>Passed by Senate February 9, 1929; 45 Stat. 1176.</p>
                <p>The debt settlement was signed at Washington May 10, 1929, by the Greek Minister
                    and the Secretary of the Treasury. The text is printed as <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Agreement Between the Governments of the Hellenic
                        Republic and the United States of America, May 10, 1929</hi>. (File No.
                    868.51 War Credits/527.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
